{
  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4688",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is shown to interact with multiple targets that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Dual specificity mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase 6 (DAMK6). The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C acts as a modulator of the signaling pathways involving Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK and LIM domain kinase 2, which are both targets of flavopiridol. Flavopiridol, in turn, is a known inhibitor of DAMK6, indicating a potential pathway through which Oblonganoside C may exert its effects. Additionally, Oblonganoside C is shown to target Cytochrome P450 2E1, which is also a target of flavopiridol, further reinforcing the link between Oblonganoside C and DAMK6 through this metabolic pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex network of interactions that Oblonganoside C may engage in, ultimately contributing to the suppression of DAMK6 activity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Oblonganoside C and DAMK6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
